      "comment": "The Byzantine fast of forty days before Christmas, from 15 November, called St Philip’s fast because it begins the day after his feast; in the West Advent takes its place. A plain Latin description: <span lang=\"la\">jējūnium</span>, a fast, is classical; <span lang=\"la\">nātīvitās</span>, birth, late (Tert.; Lewis &amp; Short)."
    }
